hdaccess: include libgen.h for basename

glibc declares a GNU basename in string.h; musl (1.2.5 on) declares only
POSIX's, in libgen.h, so hdaccess.c fails with an implicit declaration.
The device names it is given have no trailing slash, so the POSIX
version's right to modify its argument never applies.

Signed-off-by: XxI0NICxX <vifair22@gmail.com>
---
--- a/src/hdaccess.c	2024-01-05 05:40:38.000000000 -0600
+++ b/src/hdaccess.c	2026-09-27 20:55:20.888922209 -0500
@@ -106,6 +106,7 @@
 #include <stdlib.h>     /* free, atexit, posix_memalign */
 #endif
 #include <ctype.h>	/* isspace */
+#include <libgen.h>	/* basename: musl declares it only here */
 #ifdef HAVE_GLOB_H
 #include <glob.h>
 #endif
